{
 "about": "Round-10 visible-defect labels for tests/bench/studio.bench.mjs --variants plain,cover (ids from tests/bench/studio-portraits.json). Keys: none (no outfit), <garment> (outfit as before), <garment>+cover (high-collar cover variant). 1 = visible defect, 0 = clean.",
 "labeller": "Second rater: fresh AI agent instances (Claude) that did not write the code, given only the rating brief and blind review sheets (cells in a per-person random order under neutral codes A-J; no QA output, no variant names). Dev sheets: 3 raters x 9 people; test sheets: 4 raters x 8-9 people. Not human raters. The garment-geometry criterion was applied more strictly than by the round-9 rater (sack bodies, tube sleeves, pasted hands count).",
 "criteria": [
  "neck/jaw join: hole, notch or step, straight cut line beside the jaw or under the ear, sliver or blob along the jaw, flat or wrong-coloured pasted neck, background gap between hair and neck",
  "garment geometry clearly wrong at normal viewing: balloon/sack body, shoulder raised over the hair, sleeves crossing as tubes, hands pasted or spotted",
  "leftovers: fragments of the original clothes, jewellery or background (flag, chair) left on or beside the person; missing parts or holes from the matte",
  "NOT counted: the procedural/CG look of the garment itself, soft hair edges, small colour differences"
 ],
